  {"i":4607,"keep":[2],"n":"お加減はいかがですか is a common polite health phrase; addition/subtraction (加減乗除) is rare for learners"},
  {"i":4618,"keep":[],"n":"Leaning toward an opinion is a figurative extension; the word is taught for physical tilting"},
  {"i":4620,"keep":[],"n":"Fumbling one's words is colloquial slang, not taught in a communication unit"},
  {"i":4621,"keep":[],"n":"Faint hope or feeling (淡い恋) is a figurative use of the colour/taste sense"},
  {"i":4627,"keep":[],"n":"Cordial (情に厚い) is figurative and above this level; the word is taught as 'thick'"},
  {"i":4636,"keep":[3],"n":"Chapped skin (肌が荒れる) is common and fits body; unruly describes behaviour, not a character trait"},
  {"i":4640,"keep":[],"n":"Becoming intimate is a rare sense; the word is taught for approaching"},
  {"i":4645,"keep":[],"n":"The 'mind' and 'money' senses are idiomatic (懐が寂しい) and the word itself is beyond this level"},
  {"i":4657,"keep":[],"n":"Longitude and latitude is rare; learners use 経度/緯度"},
  {"i":4659,"keep":[2],"n":"Affirmative form (肯定形/肯定文) is standard grammar terminology in a language class"},
  {"i":4680,"keep":[],"n":"Pretending (平静を装う) is behaviour, not a character trait"},
  {"i":4682,"keep":[],"n":"Indisposition is a rare sense; the word is taught as displeasure"},
  {"i":4687,"keep":[],"n":"Appearance/behaviour (素振り) is not a character trait; ふりをする pretence fits actions"},
  {"i":4701,"keep":[2],"n":"In-law (義理の母) is common and taught with family"},
  {"i":4710,"keep":[3],"n":"Elaborate (凝った料理) is a common descriptive use fitting qualities"},
  {"i":4737,"keep":[],"n":"Shuttlecock is usually シャトル; this sense of 羽 is rare for learners"},
  {"i":4740,"keep":[],"n":"Letting one's guard down (気が緩む) is not an emotion unit word"},
  {"i":4741,"keep":[],"n":"Anger (雷が落ちる) is an idiom; the word is taught in weather"},
